// Change: new rule
// Title: Deno Runtime Spawns Shell Or Scripting Interpreter
// Sigma ID: d87100fd-60cc-4899-a5d0-10423873eb1d
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Andrey Pautov
// Date: 2026-05-13 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects suspicious child process execution from the Deno runtime, a behavior useful for
//   MuddyWater/Dindoor-inspired hunting.
// False positives:
//   - Developer automation using Deno to orchestrate local shell commands.
// References:
//   - https://www.threathunter.ai/blog/stryker-handala-mois-muddywater-unified-brief-detection-pack-v3
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/8eb6a7aba1c59b61b5efc5e163c762bfb6136478/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_deno_susp_child_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\deno.exe" and (FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\wscript.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\cscript.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe")
